<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Fyodor Koriatovich</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 1414</span> · <a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Fyodor Koriatovich was a Lithuanian prince of the Gediminid family who ruled <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/podolia">Podolia</a> after his brothers in the late 14th century. He resisted the authority of Grand Duke Vytautas, who drove him out around 1393 and divided Podolia between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lithuania">Lithuania</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/poland">Poland</a>. Fyodor later held lands at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mukachevo">Mukachevo</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hungary">Hungary</a>, where he died.</p></div>
